      "text": "ADULT MOUSE · LUMBAR SPINAL CORD\n\nShox2 and Chx10 electrophysiology\n\nExplore the published membrane-property summaries and the study’s alternative ways of grouping recorded neurons.\n\n171 recorded neurons\n143 Shox2 · 28 Chx10 observations\n8–25 weeks\nStudy age range · L2–L5 slices\nMean ± SD\nWhole-cell recordings · source-reported summaries\n\nReporter, firing, k-means and hierarchical groups partition the same 171-observation study pool. Group counts retain that denominator; individual animal assignments are unavailable.\n\nPublished grouping\nReporter populations · Supplementary Table 1\nFiring patterns · Supplementary Table 2\nFour k-means groups · Supplementary Table 3\nSix hierarchical groups · Supplementary Table 4\nFind a membrane property\nExport study facts\n\n12 of 12 source properties shown.\n\nSupplementary Table 1. Statistical comparisons of Shox2 and Chx10 neuronal properties presented in Figure 3. Values are published mean ± SD; statistical test and p annotations remain as printed.\nSource property\tShox2\nn = 143\tChx10\nn = 28\tSource test\tReported p\nMembrane potential [mV]\t-48.2 ± 6\t-48.2 ± 5\tU=1972\t0.9\nInput resistance [MΩ]\t711.9 ± 370\t853.5 ± 337\tU=1417\t*0.01\nTime constant [ms]\t41.5 ± 20\t39.6 ± 14\tU=1982\t0.9\nCapacitance [pF]\t69.2 ± 47\t50.7 ± 20\tU=1512\t*0.04\nRheobase [pA]\t23.3 ± 13\t20.8 ± 13\tU=1748\t0.3\nAP Threshold [mV]\t-36.3 ± 4\t-35.9 ± 4\tU=1984\t0.9\nAP Half width [ms]\t1.08 ± 0.3\t1.22 ± 0.3\tU=1339\t*0.005\nfAHP duration [ms]\t4.6 ± 1.9\t5.5 ± 2.5\tU=1434\t*0.01\nsAHP duration [ms]\t87.1 ± 65\t67.1 ± 52\tU=1773\t0.3\nfAHP amplitude\t0.28 ± 0.08\t0.26 ± 0.06\tU=1855\t0.5\nPIC on voltage [mV]\t-47.9 ± 5\t-50.2 ± 5\tt(169)=2.3\t*0.02\nF/I slope\t0.32 ± 0.2\t0.24 ± 0.1\tU=1585\t0.08\nSource field locations for this table\nAnimals, recording scope and earlier study records\nSource statements and interpretation limits\nPrimary sources and byte receipts"
